      "problem": "Write the complex number $z=2-2\\text{i}$ in exponential form.",
      "worked_solution": "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-2}{2})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{7\\pi \\text{i}/4}.\n$$",
